msgid "ISP check"
msgstr ""

msgid "Checks whether your ISP freezes game UDP and finds the TTL for the whitelist fake. It sends a few short bursts to Epic's public beacons in Frankfurt, London and Paris and takes 20-60 seconds. Do not run it during a match, and not often: probing a lot gets the address punished by the DPI."
msgstr ""

msgid "Your current TTL %d works as well, nothing to change."
msgstr ""

msgid "Now: TTL %d%s. fnport restarts; a match in progress is not affected."
msgstr ""

msgid "works from"
msgstr ""

msgid "More than 25 replies: the port passes. 20-25: the DPI froze the flow. Fewer than 20: the beacon limits replies or packets get lost. Even where the fake works, about half of the ports pass, which is enough for fnport."
msgstr ""

msgid "No clear answer: no beacon froze, but some answered only part of the packets. The beacons limit replies when asked often, or the link loses packets. Try again in 15-30 minutes."
msgstr ""

msgid "few replies"
msgstr ""

msgid "Trying the spare fake %s with TTL %d…"
msgstr ""

msgid "The ISP freezes game UDP. The first fake did not help, but the spare %s does. Recommended fake TTL: %d."
msgstr ""

msgid "Spare fake"
msgstr ""

msgid "Apply TTL %d and fake %s"
msgstr ""

msgid "%s, spare %s, TTL %d"
msgstr ""

msgid "Files with a fake QUIC Initial carrying a whitelisted SNI. One is sent before each probe and connection with a short TTL: the DPI stops freezing flows where it saw such a name. The first file is used; if it stops working, fnport switches to the next one. Empty disables the fake."
msgstr ""

msgid "Stand by where nothing freezes"
msgstr ""

msgid "If probes pass without the fake, fnport stops probing and sending the fake: connections go as they are until a frozen one shows up. What it learns is kept per network."
